  "configuration_id": "config_004",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_018 (RNA-only, scgpt, multiprofile, avgpool) achieves 0.530 acc / 0.515 F1, outperforming config_001 (multimodal, scgpt+resnet50, multiprofile, avgpool, concat) at 0.512 acc / 0.477 F1. This suggests that adding the image branch with concat fusion is actively harmful. Uncertainty: it is unclear whether the underperformance stems from the fusion strategy (concat may dilute informative RNA features with noisy image features) or from the image encoder/modality itself. Question tested: config_004 changes only the fusion from concat to weighted (keeping scgpt, resnet50, avgpool, multiprofile identical to config_001), isolating the effect of fusion. Why best next experiment: it is a clean single-variable comparison against config_001, so the result directly tells us whether the fusion mechanism is the bottleneck. If weighted fusion recovers or exceeds the RNA-only baseline, it justifies further investment in multimodal configurations with better fusion; if it does not, it shifts focus toward the image encoder or confirms RNA-only as the stronger direction—either outcome efficiently narrows the search space under limited budget."
}

